.TH LINDESK\-MCP 1 "2026" "lindesk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lindesk\-mcp \- MCP server that lets local AI agents assess and tune lindesk safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lindesk\-mcp
.RB [ \-\-stdio ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR FILTER ]
.br
.B lindesk\-mcp
.B \-\-listen
.I ADDR
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR FILTER ]
.br
.B lindesk\-mcp config
.RB [ \-\-client
.IR CLIENT ]
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR ADDR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lindesk\-mcp
is a Model Context Protocol server. A local AI agent (Claude Code, Claude Desktop,
Cursor, ...) uses it to look at the machine (status, hardware, latency map, swap,
telemetry), explain slowdowns, and apply fixes that are
.BR guardrailed ,
.B versioned
and
.BR revertible .
.PP
.B lindesk\-mcp
holds no privileges. Read-only tools probe the machine and query the telemetry lake
directly; every change goes over D-Bus to
.BR lindesk\-session (1)
(user scope) or
.BR lindeskd (8)
(system scope, polkit
.IR org.lindesk.manage ),
which validate it, record the previous values, version it and arm a dead-man switch:
a change made through MCP auto-reverts after its ttl (10 minutes by default) unless the
agent confirms it. When no daemon runs, read-only tools still work and mutating tools
return an error that says how to start one.
.PP
By default it speaks MCP over stdio, so most clients start it on demand and no service is
needed:
.PP
.RS
.B claude mcp add lindesk \-\- lindesk\-mcp
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-stdio
Serve MCP over standard input and output (the default). Logs go to stderr only.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " ADDR"
Serve MCP streamable HTTP (endpoint
.IR /mcp )
instead.
.I ADDR
is
.BI unix: PATH
(a socket created mode 0600 in a 0700 directory; no token) or a loopback
.IB IP : PORT
such as
.IR 127.0.0.1:7457 .
TCP requires
.B Authorization: Bearer
with the token generated into
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lindesk/mcp.token
(mode 0600); non-loopback addresses and requests with a browser
.B Origin
header are refused. Also read from
.BR LINDESK_MCP_LISTEN .
When started by
.I lindesk\-mcp.socket
the listening socket is inherited (socket activation).
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " FILTER"
Log filter, e.g.
.B info
or
.BR lindesk_mcp=debug .
Default:
.BR $RUST_LOG ,
else
.B warn
(stdio) or
.B info
(HTTP).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-\-client\fR claude\-code|claude\-desktop|cursor|generic] [\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIADDR\fR]
Print the snippet that registers lindesk\-mcp with an MCP client: the
.B claude mcp add
command, or the JSON for the client's configuration file. With
.BR \-\-listen ,
describe a running HTTP endpoint instead of the stdio command. Also available as
.BR "lindeskctl mcp config" .
.SH TOOLS
Read-only:
.BR status ,
.BR doctor ,
.BR hardware ,
.BR latency_map ,
.BR swap_analysis ,
.BR explain ,
.B query
(one read-only SQL statement over the telemetry lake),
.BR list_plugins ,
.BR list_profiles ,
.BR list_changes ,
.BR get_change ,
.BR recent_events ,
.B recommendations
and the dry run
.BR plan_change .
Mutating (through the daemons):
.BR apply_change ,
.BR confirm_change ,
.BR revert_change ,
.B set_profile
and
.BR calibrate .
The prompt
.B assess\-responsiveness
walks an agent through assessment, a plan, a ttl'd change, observation and confirm or
revert.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/lindesk\-mcp.socket
Optional user socket unit for a running HTTP endpoint at
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lindesk/mcp.sock .
Not enabled by default; enable it with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now lindesk\-mcp.socket" .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/lindesk\-mcp.service
The service the socket activates.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lindesk/mcp.token
Bearer token for loopback TCP.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a clean shutdown, 1 on an error (which is printed on stderr).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
claude mcp add lindesk \-\- lindesk\-mcp
lindesk\-mcp config \-\-client claude\-desktop
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now lindesk\-mcp.socket
lindesk\-mcp \-\-listen 127.0.0.1:7457
lindeskctl mcp status
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lindeskctl (1),
.BR lindeskctl\-mcp (1),
.BR lindeskctl\-changes (1),
.BR lindesk\-session (1),
.BR lindeskd (8)
